      "writtenOn": "2026-06-01T18:57:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I changed it to `uint32_t offset \u003d 0;`\n\n`uint32_t offset \u003d FP_SENSOR_IMAGE_SIZE - FP_SENSOR_IMAGE_OFFSET - size;` is not always true. The changes I made later for the `IMAGE_OFFSET` in the simulated board dts file mimic the FPC scenario. In the FPC case, there is 400 offset + image + 220 left over. So placing `offset \u003d FP_SENSOR_IMAGE_SIZE - FP_SENSOR_IMAGE_OFFSET - size;` can cause the `get_frame` command to fail.\n\nThe concern about `3 * kMaxReadSize;` is resolved by going with the first chunk.",
